.TH WMNOTIFY-SEND 1 "wm-desktop" "wm-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmnotify-send \- send a desktop notification from a script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmnotify-send
[\fIoptions\fR] \fISUMMARY\fR [\fIBODY\fR]
.br
.B wmnotify-send \-H
[\fICOUNT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A small notify-send replacement that talks to any notification daemon over D-Bus. It prints the new
notification's id when \fB\-p\fR is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-a " app"
Application name.
.TP
.BI \-i " icon"
Icon name or file path.
.TP
.BI \-u " level"
low, normal or critical.
.TP
.BI \-t " ms"
Timeout in milliseconds; 0 never expires, \-1 lets the daemon choose.
.TP
.BI \-r " id"
Replace an existing notification.
.TP
.B \-p
Print the notification id.
.TP
.BI \-v " 0..100"
Show a progress bar.
.TP
.BI \-A " key=label"
Add an action button. Can be repeated. With \fB\-w\fR the chosen key is printed.
.TP
.BI \-R " key=command"
Run a shell command when that action is picked. Implies \fB\-w\fR; the exit status is the command's.
.TP
.B \-e
Close the notification when this process exits.
.TP
.B \-w
Wait until the notification is closed or an action is picked.
.TP
.B \-H \fR[\fICOUNT\fR]
Print the last COUNT (default 20) notifications wmnotify received, including hidden ones.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
wmnotify\-send \-a backup \-A open=Open \-R "open=xdg\-open ~/backups" "Backup finished" "3 GB copied"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmnotify (1),
.BR wmnotifyctl (1)
